urposefully sabotage the show if anyone  is purposely sabotaging the show it's  the bbc as a whole not cri not chris  chibnall in specific and i'm not saying  the bbc is purposely sabotaging doctor  who but i am saying that the decisions  being made at a higher level than chris  jamil had control over by the bbc were  detrimental to this show that i think is  kind of indisputable and the other thing  is  for as much as i  have and will continue to criticize this  era of doctor who  it's gotten us some good stuff  some good characters  some good beats some good episodes even  if i'm gonna say in defense of chris  chibnall i should probably cite some  specific things that i really enjoy  there are specific characters and  casting decisions that i think work  really well  graham was great dan i ended up liking a  heck of a lot more than i thought  considering i really desperately did not  want another  modern time companion to be joining i  especially didn't want another one  joining in on yaz and the doctor when i  wanted to see that relationship be built  up more but  i like dan he won me over i really like  sasha dewan as the master i  love joe martin as the fugitive doctor  which is another thing that i think kind  of suffered under the  changing in shooting how many episodes  they were going to get the way they had  to shoot etc  i have little doubt that  there was an original plan to do a lot  more with the fugitive doctor than we  got and i want  i wanted and i still want so much more  from her  but  you know after series 12 introduced her  if she was supposed to show up more in  flux and or after that  well  everything i've already talked about  with the shooting of flux we've even had  some good villains i really like ashad  i think he's a fantastic concept and an  amazing performance he's a really good  villain and i'm kind of excited that  we're going to see him again in the  final episode now  if i'm being honest most of my favorite  episodes of this era  weren't written by chibnall at least not  on his own they were either written by  other people or were co-written by  chibnall but  that having been said they were still  made under his tenure as show runner he  fostered these stories he helped them  come about so he deserves at least some  credit for the fact that i got things  like it takes you away  can you hear me war of the centaurus  honestly even eve at the daleks i think  that's probably the best one that he  himself wrote it was fun and energetic  and a neat use of a time loop which is  something that doctor who has not done  very much you think it would have been a  time travel show but  that was good  war of the sun tyrants might honestly be  my favorite sontaran specific story of  the modern era the idea of using the  historical settings to put more of a  focus on eras and the things going on on  a bigger scale and a little bit less  emphasis on individuals even though a  lot of times they were still there i  think that's the case with rosa that's  definitely the case with demons of the  punjab and look don't get me wrong  i'm not sad he's leaving  that that was never in the cards but you  know given the fact that i've spent the  last three or four years largely bashing  on the guy  i think it would be unfair for me not to  acknowledge  there's been some good here and that  some of the things he tried  are things i probably would have tried  and or support in theory even if the  execution wasn't there  i don't think that about every decision  he made but  it's important to be fair  so i call this a defense of chris  chibnall  i mean maybe it's not really maybe it's  more of a  let's be fair to chris chibnall  but that's not a nice clickbaity title  so i couldn't go with that  but yeah  i [ __ ] a lot  on this channel i know that  especially when it comes to doctor who i  can be real picky but  i don't want anyone to ever forget that  i love this show  and there have been moments within  even chibnall's time that i have loved  so in the spirit of positivity  what is your favorite thing about  chibnalzera  it can be a bit of casting specific  episode specific general idea it can  even be something that you love that i  hate it's all on the table whatever you  think was good  about his time as showrunner  drop something down in the comments  let's talk about it oh and please don't  be the needless contrarian who's just  gonna go there was nothing good like  work with me in the spirit of this okay  if that's all you've got to say just  don't  but uh  i do wanna hear your thoughts  i wanna know what people liked  whether it's what i liked or not  if you want to support what i can do  patreon is how i make my living and i'm  able to do this full-time as my job any  amount you can contribute helps but  there are other things you can do as  well like share subscribe help out this  channel quite a bit the algorithm is  very up and down on me lately uh it  hasn't been consistent for me in a while  um but also there's other things you can  check me out and i'm on twitch tiktok  instagram i have books for sale  fictional and non-fiction  but uh  you don't have to worry too much  about any of that  because what i really want you to  remember  in the spirit of positivity  is that you are beautiful  you are valid  and you are loved  you are the council i'm just running the  meetings and until next time this  council  is adjourned  [Music]  and credits i gotta shout out my top  patreon supporters so thank you very  much to zubin luthfulla barack oliver  bean melinda walters lyotha boy tt for  knobby lax the poodle idol tracy  scrabbat vincent paul bartolucci angry  casper adam lefty taylor shane ross  robin moore shayla gourlay and brendan  the rose  couldn't do it without you  [Music]  [Music]  so  [Music]  um  [Music]
 

